{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792442740,"nonce":"uvWaNMCq8/gAzsX2YABHXi2X2a8=","message":"Current Ashui pin 4bbb99a93d1ff2d5a37826ac28ab0608f3cd2199 retains a regression introduced by 247cc4e: CodeLine.indexOfKind only maps the eleven built-in CodeTokenKind strings, with no fallback for custom strings. RayDE OutputHighlighter emits output-error, output-warning and output-success, scoped by CSS to .rayde-output. Packing loses those names, so the Git snapshot assertion \"Git error lost its severity in Output\" now fails on the real no-remote Fetch error.\n\nMinimal reproduction (also fails with haxe --interp):\n\nvar line = new ashui.components.code.CodeDocument.CodeLine(\"Git error\");\nline.tokens = [{from:0, to:9, kind:cast \"output-error\"}];\nSys.println(haxe.Json.stringify(line.tokens));\n\nExpected: the output-error kind round-trips. Actual under --interp: Null Access at CodeDocument.hx:63; the native snapshot loses the expected output-error kind. Please preserve custom token strings when packing, for example by interning additional kinds alongside the built-ins. Output severity coloring is blocked until this is fixed.\n\nFound while verifying sidebar resize fixes. Separate proven causes of the resize blinking are in RayDE: object keys rebuilding the sidebar on every treeWidth invalidation, followed by one-frame delayed canvas dimensions written in settledHooks. Neither requires an Ashui change. The sidebar retention and direct percentage canvas sizing changes pass the frame-by-frame resize assertions.","files":null}]}